row(22, 17, 'MATERIAL', f'AND BEHOLD, HE LAYS A CHARGE OF WORDS, SAYING: I FOUND NO TOKENS IN YOUR DAUGHTER — AND THESE ARE MY DAUGHTER\'S TOKENS; AND THEY SPREAD THE GARMENT BEFORE THE ELDERS OF THE CITY. {HP(22, 17, (("ואלה", "בתולי", "בתי"), "and these are my daughter\'s tokens — 236:1\'s counter-witnesses"), (("ופרשו", "השמלה", "לפני", "זקני", "העיר"), "and they spread the garment before the elders — 237\'s three readings"))} {AP(22, 17, (("ויפרסון", "שושיפא", "קדם", "סבי", "קרתא"), "AND THEY SPREAD THE SHEET (shoshipa) BEFORE THE ELDERS OF THE CITY — the garment a specific cloth in the Aramaic, R. Eliezer b. Jacob\'s letter (237:3)"))} the chapter\'s one "saying". Fresh.')
